<!--
  AbxrLib IL2CPP managed-code-stripping preservation.

  Unity's IL2CPP linker strips managed types it cannot see referenced from code. AbxrLib's
  AppConfig ScriptableObject is loaded via Resources.Load and has no direct code reference, so on
  IL2CPP builds with managed stripping enabled (Medium or higher) it gets pruned. At runtime that
  shows up as "The referenced script ... is missing!", the config deserializes empty, and
  initialization fails with "App identification not set".

  This reproduces on Unity 2021.3 (Unity 6 auto-preserves asset-referenced types, masking it).
  Preserving the runtime assembly keeps every AbxrLib type regardless of the consumer project's
  Managed Stripping Level. Editor and Tests assemblies are excluded on purpose - they are never in
  player builds.

  The world-space objects (keyboard, PIN pad, exit poll, QR) ship their own link.xml, because once
  imported they are compiled from the project's Assets folder and are not part of this package.

  Unity automatically detects link.xml files inside a package, so no setup or relocation is
  required by the consuming project.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="AbxrLib.Runtime" preserve="all" />
</linker>
